1
00:00:01,020 --> 00:00:02,020
Takaaki.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:04,580
This is my order.

3
00:00:05,790 --> 00:00:09,300
Deal a fatal blow to my father's company.

4
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:13,740
Understood.

5
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:16,430
As long as I don't use violence,

6
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:19,880
I can use any means necessary
to crush it completely, right?

7
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:21,620
Of course.

8
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,740
No need to show any mercy.

9
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,040
You can handle this, right?

10
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:30,480
Yeah.

11
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
"The Servant Prince" (Episode 8)

12
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:32,550
Yes.

13
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,480
If you leave the entire strategy to us,

14
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:41,260
yes, we guarantee you'll win the bid.

15
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:44,830
We're counting on you, then.

16
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:46,930
Got it.

17
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:48,580
That's all for now.

18
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:00,530
I won't let you have your way.

19
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:05,160
Excuse me.

20
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:09,750
President.

21
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,959
Regarding Goto Construction's core system,

22
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:14,210
It seems it's still riddled with bugs.

23
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,669
Their technical debt has
ballooned out of control.

24
00:02:16,670 --> 00:02:19,430
I hear it's gotten to the point where
no company dares to take it on.

25
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:20,760
I figured as much.

26
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:24,520
They already lost their
credibility due to the data leak.

27
00:02:24,970 --> 00:02:27,170
To think they still haven't
found a way to bounce back.

28
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:28,480
Yes.

29
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:33,899
How is the station building
project coming along?

30
00:02:33,900 --> 00:02:35,780
Ah, about that.

31
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:39,460
Just as you predicted, President,
the bidding is merely a formality.

32
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:43,970
In reality, Goto Construction has
already been chosen behind closed doors.

33
00:02:45,830 --> 00:02:48,470
If they knew about Goto
Construction's current internal situation,

34
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:50,850
this deal would fall through, too.

35
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:55,560
Next, we just need to set up a competitor
to replace Goto Construction.

36
00:02:55,840 --> 00:02:57,640
And have them
successfully enter the bidding.

37
00:02:58,170 --> 00:02:59,170
Understood.

38
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:02,690
Any other orders?

39
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:10,290
Orders?

40
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:18,030
This order is the most
fired up I've ever been.

41
00:03:19,530 --> 00:03:20,530
Excuse me?

42
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:24,070
Never mind. I was just talking to myself.

43
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,220
Understood.

44
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,830
I'll take my leave now.

45
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:55,830
I've always wanted
to lock Naoya up.

46
00:03:57,070 --> 00:04:01,570
So that I would be the
only thing in his world.

47
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:04,740
That's right.

48
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:07,720
Like keeping a frail little bird in a cage.

49
00:04:08,870 --> 00:04:11,390
Maybe that's what would give
me the most peace of mind.

50
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:17,750
But Naoya stood up on his own two feet.

51
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:19,880
I...

52
00:04:21,050 --> 00:04:22,370
I'm going to get a part-time job.

53
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:27,430
And then, he flew out of
that room full of energy.

54
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,810
We'll be living here starting today.

55
00:04:30,660 --> 00:04:31,730
Just the two of us.

56
00:04:34,810 --> 00:04:40,190
The Naoya I could lock in my embrace
is no longer here.

57
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:54,260
Good morning.

58
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:58,640
Good morning.

59
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,440
Are you okay?

60
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,560
I just feel...

61
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:08,450
So powerless.

62
00:05:08,970 --> 00:05:09,970
Huh?

63
00:05:10,940 --> 00:05:15,140
I tried negotiating with upper
management after that, but it was no use.

64
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:19,206
Even though Mori-san said
after he gets back from his trip abroad,

65
00:05:19,230 --> 00:05:21,950
he'd be willing to come back to
work under the re-employment system.

66
00:05:22,570 --> 00:05:26,170
In the end, a store manager is
nothing more than an on-site coordinator.

67
00:05:26,910 --> 00:05:28,910
Just one word from the
higher-ups at headquarters,

68
00:05:28,940 --> 00:05:31,510
and this store we worked so hard
to build up together,

69
00:05:32,410 --> 00:05:34,250
can be taken away in an instant.

70
00:05:40,090 --> 00:05:41,090
Manager.

71
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:42,750
I'm truly sorry.

72
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:45,440
Wait, why are you apologizing?

73
00:05:45,470 --> 00:05:46,970
This isn't your fault, Goto-kun.

74
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:49,390
I'm really grateful to you.

75
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,570
Please, raise your head.

76
00:05:52,930 --> 00:05:53,930
Anyway,

77
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:56,950
Until we close down,
please keep working hard with us.

78
00:05:57,350 --> 00:05:58,560
I'm counting on you.

79
00:06:00,060 --> 00:06:01,060
Manager...

80
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:07,960
Manager, I haven't given up yet.

81
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:12,090
Since it's come to this,
let's prove it to them with our sales.

82
00:06:12,330 --> 00:06:12,950
Huh?

83
00:06:12,990 --> 00:06:16,660
Let's make our sales and reviews
number one among all the branches.

84
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:18,040
Goto-kun...

85
00:06:19,370 --> 00:06:20,540
He's right.

86
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:26,170
I'll show them the kitchen's grit, too.

87
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:31,090
I'll keep providing the best service
right down to the very last customer.

88
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:35,460
Let's make headquarters regret
ever wanting to close such a great store.

89
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:36,830
Everyone...

90
00:06:36,850 --> 00:06:37,850
Manager.

91
00:06:38,310 --> 00:06:40,810
Let's show them what we're made of.

92
00:06:41,310 --> 00:06:42,310
Yeah.

93
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:47,899
All right, let's leave the
higher-ups speechless.

94
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:52,200
Yeah, let's do this!

95
00:06:52,260 --> 00:06:53,599
Let's give it our all!

96
00:06:53,600 --> 00:06:56,920
Here is your dessert,
our seasonal cake.

97
00:06:56,940 --> 00:06:57,940
Please enjoy.

98
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:02,020
I can't just bark orders at Takaaki.

99
00:07:02,670 --> 00:07:06,210
I have to do everything in my power, too.

100
00:07:06,660 --> 00:07:08,129
- Would you like me to pour this for you?
- Yes, please.

101
00:07:08,130 --> 00:07:09,060
Certainly. Excuse me.

102
00:07:09,061 --> 00:07:10,550
Yes, right away.

103
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:14,640
Thank you for waiting.

104
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:19,019
Nishida, just add the
demi-glaze sauce and it's done.

105
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:20,020
Got it.

106
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:23,212
Regarding the restaurant
"Luore" and Unicolla,

107
00:07:23,266 --> 00:07:23,872
[Goto Construction]

108
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:26,480
Both are proceeding according
to your instructions, President.

109
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:28,540
I see.

110
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:31,060
However, President,

111
00:07:32,450 --> 00:07:34,410
Is this really okay?

112
00:07:38,910 --> 00:07:39,910
What?

113
00:07:40,210 --> 00:07:40,910
Nothing.

114
00:07:40,911 --> 00:07:42,000
Tanizawa.

115
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:45,340
If you have the free
time to talk back to me,

116
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,940
You'd be better off securing
a system vendor to replace Unicolla.

117
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:54,760
If the system isn't fixed, our
company's credibility can't be restored.

118
00:07:55,930 --> 00:07:56,930
Yes, sir.

119
00:07:56,970 --> 00:08:00,390
Besides, this is a critical
moment before the bidding.

120
00:08:01,850 --> 00:08:02,890
The issue with the system,

121
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:06,440
keep a tight lid on it.
It absolutely must not leak to the outside.

122
00:08:07,270 --> 00:08:08,740
Understood.

123
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:24,630
I see.

124
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:27,750
That station building
project is, to my dad...

125
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:31,520
No... to Goto Construction,
it's their biggest lifeline.

126
00:08:32,510 --> 00:08:35,050
If we strike there,
we can deal them a fatal blow.

127
00:08:36,010 --> 00:08:37,100
Hit them hard.

128
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:38,890
Understood.

129
00:08:39,390 --> 00:08:41,100
I'll execute it flawlessly.

130
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:46,820
Ah...

131
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:50,900
Yuma.

132
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:01,870
I figured this was the case.

133
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:04,850
You figured it out?

134
00:09:05,360 --> 00:09:06,960
Figured out that Father was behind this.

135
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:08,500
Yeah.

136
00:09:09,380 --> 00:09:12,420
But honestly,
I never thought he'd go this far.

137
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:17,220
After all, before getting in my way,

138
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:20,790
As the top executive, shouldn't he figure
out how to manage his own company first?

139
00:09:21,930 --> 00:09:25,790
That just shows how much
Father cares about you.

140
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,720
Huh?

141
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:31,020
Father must be terrified of your abilities.

142
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,780
If he lets you do as you please,

143
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:37,590
You'll definitely achieve
greater things than him.

144
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:39,930
He wants to stop that from happening.

145
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:46,830
To keep you from succeeding, he deliberately
pushes difficult problems onto you.

146
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,710
He wants to make you submit to him.

147
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:51,340
He wants to keep you
close so he can watch you.

148
00:09:54,420 --> 00:09:55,920
It's a terrifying obsession.

149
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:58,320
It's enough to make your skin crawl.

150
00:10:01,060 --> 00:10:05,950
In contrast, I've only ever been
treated as your replacement.

151
00:10:09,220 --> 00:10:10,310
Someone like me...

152
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,630
Is just a tool he uses to provoke you.

153
00:10:17,530 --> 00:10:19,260
Even though I'm a part of the company, too,

154
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:21,760
Father refuses to listen to a word I say.

155
00:10:22,490 --> 00:10:23,990
Father is wrong right now.

156
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:27,810
Everyone in the company is fed up, too.
Morale is falling apart.

157
00:10:31,780 --> 00:10:35,260
Yuma, do you remember the
subsidiary I used to manage?

158
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:41,070
Right before they went bankrupt, I used my final
authority to transfer them back to headquarters.

159
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:45,070
They will definitely
be a great help to you.

160
00:10:45,890 --> 00:10:47,430
Go gather your allies, Yuma.

161
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:49,950
Build your own faction.

162
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:53,020
To stand up against our dad.

163
00:10:53,610 --> 00:10:55,440
Then come back, brother.

164
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:58,030
Those people are your allies, right?

165
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:00,530
Please.

166
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,950
I'm at my limit doing this alone.

167
00:11:06,660 --> 00:11:07,660
No.

168
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:10,930
I'm not going back.

169
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,460
That's how it is.

170
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,960
I'm going to live my life with him.

171
00:11:42,990 --> 00:11:44,420
Right, Takaaki?

172
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,370
Yeah, of course.

173
00:11:52,790 --> 00:11:53,790
It'll be fine.

174
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:56,000
You can definitely do it.

175
00:11:57,120 --> 00:12:01,860
The one to shoulder the future of
Goto Construction is you, Yuma.

176
00:12:15,070 --> 00:12:16,070
After that,

177
00:12:16,390 --> 00:12:19,150
Thanks to the competitor
Takaaki arranged entering the bid,

178
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:22,449
Goto Construction hit rock bottom.

179
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:23,490
Why?

180
00:12:24,200 --> 00:12:25,780
Why did it turn out like this?

181
00:12:26,150 --> 00:12:30,249
That station building project
was already internally decided to be ours.

182
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:34,249
Our company's system
vulnerabilities still haven't been fixed.

183
00:12:34,250 --> 00:12:35,629
That's the root of it all.

184
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:37,869
That's why I said we
needed to handle it ASAP.

185
00:12:37,870 --> 00:12:42,469
But President, the only ones who can rebuild
that massive system in a short time...

186
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,470
Is Unicolla. We have no other choice.

187
00:12:44,800 --> 00:12:45,820
So,

188
00:12:45,930 --> 00:12:48,989
Which company beat us to the bid?

189
00:12:48,990 --> 00:12:50,220
It was Amagi Construction.

190
00:12:50,610 --> 00:12:52,019
By the way, intelligence indicates that

191
00:12:52,020 --> 00:12:54,810
Their system maintenance has
already been handed over to Unicolla.

192
00:12:54,850 --> 00:12:56,730
That guy's company again?

193
00:12:58,110 --> 00:13:01,440
Furthermore, led by your
younger brother Yuma,

194
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:03,800
the anti-president faction
has banded together.

195
00:13:04,890 --> 00:13:06,950
As the company's performance deteriorated,

196
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:10,370
Dad's unifying power completely collapsed.

197
00:13:15,990 --> 00:13:19,210
And as for the restaurant "Luore,"

198
00:13:21,380 --> 00:13:25,259
Thanks to everyone,
our sales ranked number one.

199
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:27,489
That's great!

200
00:13:27,490 --> 00:13:29,559
We really showed them what we're made of.

201
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:30,430
Yes.

202
00:13:30,431 --> 00:13:33,160
I have one more thing to report.

203
00:13:33,670 --> 00:13:34,670
This store...

204
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:37,520
Has been confirmed to stay open.

205
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,626
(Notice of Store Closure Cancellation)
Really?

206
00:13:39,650 --> 00:13:40,859
That's amazing!

207
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:42,569
Thank goodness!

208
00:13:42,570 --> 00:13:46,069
However, in exchange, the Mita branch,
which has seen declining sales recently,

209
00:13:46,070 --> 00:13:48,370
Will be merged into our store.

210
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:50,280
Then our understaffing issue...

211
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:51,740
Will be solved.

212
00:13:52,550 --> 00:13:55,660
Thank you all so much.

213
00:13:57,430 --> 00:13:58,430
Goto-kun.

214
00:13:58,910 --> 00:14:01,460
It's all thanks to you not giving up.

215
00:14:01,890 --> 00:14:03,170
I really appreciate it.

216
00:14:03,610 --> 00:14:04,610
Thank you.

217
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Don't mention it.

218
00:14:06,870 --> 00:14:08,760
Let's keep working hard together.

219
00:14:09,070 --> 00:14:10,930
Mori-san will be back soon, too.

220
00:14:11,190 --> 00:14:12,190
Yeah.

221
00:14:12,670 --> 00:14:15,489
Alright, everyone together.
Ready?

222
00:14:15,490 --> 00:14:18,310
Let's do this!

223
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:22,730
Anyway,
the restaurant can stay open.

224
00:14:23,470 --> 00:14:24,570
That's wonderful news.

225
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:27,950
Yuma has been working really hard, too.

226
00:14:28,570 --> 00:14:31,200
He took the lead in forming a new faction.

227
00:14:31,450 --> 00:14:34,640
I heard all the top employees, especially
the younger ones, are following him.

228
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:36,160
I see.

229
00:14:37,030 --> 00:14:39,580
Dad probably doesn't have
a single ally left by his side.

230
00:14:40,670 --> 00:14:44,940
It's going to be the era of a brand new
Goto Construction built by Yuma.

231
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:48,930
Yeah, he'll definitely do a great job.

232
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:53,740
Takaaki, thank you so much.

233
00:14:55,470 --> 00:14:56,470
No.

234
00:14:57,730 --> 00:15:02,520
I only acted
because of your orders.

235
00:15:06,030 --> 00:15:10,030
Your orders mean everything to me.
They are my reason for living.

236
00:15:12,390 --> 00:15:13,390
Takaaki.

237
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:16,790
Yeah.

238
00:15:38,810 --> 00:15:40,870
So that's how it is.

239
00:15:42,410 --> 00:15:46,610
Two grown men acting like this.
How disgraceful.

240
00:15:47,370 --> 00:15:48,370
Those words.

241
00:15:49,030 --> 00:15:50,680
I'll return them right back to you.

242
00:15:52,660 --> 00:15:53,660
What?

243
00:15:53,910 --> 00:15:55,870
Mom was the only one
who thought of you that way.

244
00:15:56,450 --> 00:15:59,000
The only one who found your
pathetic behavior endearing.

245
00:16:00,190 --> 00:16:03,880
No one will ever feel
that way about you again.

246
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:06,670
Never again.

247
00:16:10,250 --> 00:16:12,570
Blinded by short-term gains,

248
00:16:12,800 --> 00:16:14,430
you neglected cybersecurity.

249
00:16:15,930 --> 00:16:17,890
As the leader of an organization,

250
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:21,580
it seems you've completely lost sight of
what you should truly be protecting.

251
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:27,040
What does a nouveau
riche brat like you know?

252
00:16:28,310 --> 00:16:30,190
I offered you such a high price.

253
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:32,400
Why did you refuse?

254
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:42,260
You were the one who canceled the contract
in the first place, President Goto.

255
00:16:46,510 --> 00:16:48,940
Did you really think
the person you cast aside

256
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:52,570
would still lend you a helping hand now?

257
00:17:13,270 --> 00:17:14,380
Please.

258
00:17:16,810 --> 00:17:17,950
Help me.

259
00:17:19,530 --> 00:17:24,450
At this rate,
everything I've built...

260
00:17:25,460 --> 00:17:27,750
Goto Construction is going to go bankrupt.

261
00:17:29,710 --> 00:17:30,710
Please.

262
00:17:33,770 --> 00:17:35,030
I'm begging you.

263
00:17:41,850 --> 00:17:42,910
I refuse.

264
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:54,800
Because I only take orders from him.

265
00:18:08,880 --> 00:18:11,060
Go visit my mother's grave first.

266
00:18:12,430 --> 00:18:14,480
And apologize for everything you've done.

267
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:18,010
If you do that, I'll ask him to help.

268
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:24,680
Understood.

269
00:18:35,690 --> 00:18:36,750
Enjoy your meal.

270
00:18:57,550 --> 00:19:02,900
I plan to take over Goto Construction
properly in Dad's place.

271
00:19:05,650 --> 00:19:08,440
Because your allies
are all on my side.

272
00:19:10,190 --> 00:19:14,830
Having such reliable partners
is all thanks to you.

273
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,030
No.

274
00:19:19,970 --> 00:19:21,820
It's because you worked so hard.

275
00:19:23,610 --> 00:19:25,430
That's why everyone is following you.

276
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:29,830
They are now officially

277
00:19:32,210 --> 00:19:33,430
your allies.

278
00:19:33,470 --> 00:19:34,470
Yuma.

279
00:19:36,990 --> 00:19:38,230
You're right.

280
00:19:40,490 --> 00:19:44,389
You now have a one-of-a-kind,
invincible expert

281
00:19:44,390 --> 00:19:45,970
backing you up.

282
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:48,230
I can't afford to lose either.

283
00:19:49,530 --> 00:19:50,530
Yeah.

284
00:19:52,130 --> 00:19:53,650
Maybe so.

285
00:20:00,780 --> 00:20:02,490
An invincible expert?

286
00:20:02,610 --> 00:20:04,070
That's what Yuma said.

287
00:20:04,410 --> 00:20:06,430
He said you are
one of a kind to me.

288
00:20:07,130 --> 00:20:08,130
No.

289
00:20:08,610 --> 00:20:10,080
I'm not that amazing.

290
00:20:10,330 --> 00:20:13,710
But the moment you took over the system,

291
00:20:13,950 --> 00:20:17,250
Dad's bankrupt company
came back to life.

292
00:20:17,850 --> 00:20:19,440
So maybe Yuma was right.

293
00:20:20,670 --> 00:20:22,110
I'll be counting on you from now on.

294
00:20:22,510 --> 00:20:24,300
My very own expert.

295
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:25,970
Yeah, I understand.

296
00:20:29,350 --> 00:20:31,410
Can I ask you something?

297
00:20:32,730 --> 00:20:36,320
Why did you order me
to save his company?

298
00:20:39,270 --> 00:20:41,550
Don't you hate your father
from the bottom of your heart?

299
00:20:46,070 --> 00:20:47,070
Yeah.

300
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:50,260
I hate him.

301
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:54,670
Even now.

302
00:20:57,170 --> 00:21:00,800
But rather than sending
him straight to hell,

303
00:21:01,010 --> 00:21:03,590
I wanted him to choose
a more painful way to live.

304
00:21:04,550 --> 00:21:06,140
Even if the company is rebuilt,

305
00:21:06,670 --> 00:21:08,660
I want him to live all alone

306
00:21:08,760 --> 00:21:10,430
and taste absolute despair.

307
00:21:11,810 --> 00:21:15,650
Mom is no longer by his side.

308
00:21:17,130 --> 00:21:22,820
He single-handedly destroyed the only
person who loved him unconditionally.

309
00:21:26,670 --> 00:21:31,850
I hope this becomes Dad's
most irreversible regret.

310
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:37,330
That might indeed be
the cruelest punishment.

311
00:21:40,570 --> 00:21:41,570
Yeah.

312
00:21:48,180 --> 00:21:50,100
I won't end up like Dad.

313
00:21:52,170 --> 00:21:53,270
So, Takaaki,

314
00:21:54,270 --> 00:21:55,850
please stay by my side forever.

315
00:21:59,910 --> 00:22:00,940
Understood.

316
00:22:01,450 --> 00:22:02,450
Hey.

317
00:22:02,810 --> 00:22:04,700
This isn't one of my usual orders.

318
00:22:05,230 --> 00:22:07,360
I want to hear your true feelings.

319
00:22:11,910 --> 00:22:13,160
I know.

320
00:22:14,660 --> 00:22:16,370
I want to be with you forever, too.

321
00:22:17,490 --> 00:22:18,750
With you, Naoya.

322
00:22:25,470 --> 00:22:26,510
Yeah.

323
00:22:55,990 --> 00:22:57,500
Can I give you an order?

324
00:22:58,890 --> 00:22:59,890
Of course.

325
00:23:00,750 --> 00:23:02,710
You've been working too hard.

326
00:23:03,130 --> 00:23:05,340
Take some time off
and go on a trip with me.

327
00:23:07,220 --> 00:23:08,300
Understood.

328
00:23:43,210 --> 00:23:44,170
Alright.

329
00:23:44,171 --> 00:23:47,130
Takaaki, let's go.

330
00:23:47,510 --> 00:23:48,550
Okay.

331
00:23:49,810 --> 00:23:51,609
Is camping okay for our trip?

332
00:23:51,610 --> 00:23:52,340
Yeah.

333
00:23:52,470 --> 00:23:54,760
Deep in the mountains
where there's zero cell service.

334
00:23:55,350 --> 00:23:56,350
Huh?

335
00:23:56,430 --> 00:23:58,680
If there's a signal, you'll
just end up working again.

336
00:24:01,610 --> 00:24:02,770
Okay.

337
00:24:02,810 --> 00:24:05,610
Today, we're going to
eat camp food together.

338
00:24:07,190 --> 00:24:11,700
Then, we'll take our time
talking by the campfire.

339
00:24:13,660 --> 00:24:14,530
Understood.
Yeah.

340
00:24:18,700 --> 00:24:19,700
Oh?

341
00:24:22,290 --> 00:24:23,290
What's wrong?

342
00:24:23,790 --> 00:24:24,670
Be careful.

343
00:24:24,710 --> 00:24:25,710
Sorry.

344
00:24:30,790 --> 00:24:32,386
(Special Episode Preview)
Takaaki, make the rain stop.

345
00:24:32,410 --> 00:24:33,799
Stop the rain.

346
00:24:33,800 --> 00:24:36,049
Oh, that's nice.

347
00:24:36,050 --> 00:24:37,050
This is absolutely amazing.

348
00:24:37,051 --> 00:24:41,139
It feels great being the only one
who knows his hidden side.

349
00:24:41,140 --> 00:24:44,430
You've truly met a wonderful person,
Goto-san.
